WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.268 --> 00:00:16.729
dare you accuse me!"

2
00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.772
John exclaimed as everyone else gasped.

3
00:00:19.792 --> 00:00:22.513
"You can't prove anything!"

4
00:00:22.533 --> 00:00:26.836
"I can't prove you dumped those frogs," Henry said.

5
00:00:26.856 --> 00:00:30.699
"But I know you poured the paint in Kyle's bag.

6
00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:35.841
Kyle, Coach Phillips, and I were the only ones who looked at the paint.

7
00:00:36.862 --> 00:00:39.123
But you just said it was green paint.

8
00:00:40.583 --> 00:00:43.965
How would you know that unless you poured it in there yourself?"

9
00:00:45.125 --> 00:00:46.066
Daisy gasped.

10
00:00:46.086 --> 00:00:49.227
"He did say it was green!"

11
00:00:49.247 --> 00:00:53.609
"That was just a lucky guess," John protested.

12
00:00:53.629 --> 00:00:57.891
"Daisy is always painting pictures of trees and stuff.

13
00:00:59.071 --> 00:01:00.912
I figured she'd use green paint!"

14
00:01:01.912 --> 00:01:03.313
But the coach was frowning.

15
00:01:03.333 --> 00:01:07.195
"Did you have anything to do with those frogs, John?"

16
00:01:07.575 --> 00:01:08.215
he asked.

17
00:01:09.796 --> 00:01:12.958
"His parents own a pet store," Tiny spoke up.

18
00:01:12.978 --> 00:01:18.301
"I bet he got the frogs there and dumped them in the pool when we weren't looking!"

19
00:01:18.321 --> 00:01:21.603
"I just remembered something," Cole said.

20
00:01:21.623 --> 00:01:24.724
"John was the fastest jogger.

21
00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:27.766
He got back to the pool before the rest of us."

22
00:01:28.907 --> 00:01:30.928
"I remember that too," Kyle said.

23
00:01:31.972 --> 00:01:33.313
"Cole and I got there next.

24
00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:36.515
But it took us a few more minutes than John.

25
00:01:37.736 --> 00:01:40.378
He had plenty of time to dump the frogs back in the water."

26
00:01:40.398 --> 00:01:45.081
"And place my flip-flops near the buckets," Cole added.

27
00:01:46.202 --> 00:01:47.603
Tommy stared at his brother.

28
00:01:47.623 --> 00:01:52.387
"Is that why you said you'd go inside and get Tiny's towel for Daisy, John?"

29
00:01:52.407 --> 00:01:55.269
"Aha!" Henry said.

30
00:01:55.289 --> 00:01:59.232
"So John was behind the ant trick too!"

31
00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:03.042
Finally John hid his face in his hands.

32
00:02:03.062 --> 00:02:05.264
"Okay, you're right.

33
00:02:05.284 --> 00:02:06.304
It was all me!"

34
00:02:06.725 --> 00:02:07.485
he blurted out.

35
00:02:07.505 --> 00:02:11.529
"I stained the towel and dragged it through an anthill.

36
00:02:12.710 --> 00:02:17.193
Then I folded it so nobody would notice the ants until Daisy used the towel.

37
00:02:18.354 --> 00:02:20.176
I dumped the frogs in the pool too.

38
00:02:21.377 --> 00:02:22.097
I'm sorry.

39
00:02:22.117 --> 00:02:27.121
I thought if I got rid of everyone else, Tommy might make the team."

40
00:02:28.683 --> 00:02:29.944
Tommy stared at John.

41
00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:32.120
"Why would you do that?

42
00:02:33.161 --> 00:02:34.921
You know I don't care much about swimming."

43
00:02:34.941 --> 00:02:41.723
"If you don't make the swim team, Mom and Dad will let you take tennis lessons instead," John

44
00:02:41.803 --> 00:02:45.824
said. "I heard them talking about how expensive that is.

45
00:02:46.964 --> 00:02:50.385
They might not have enough money to buy me a car for my birthday!"

46
00:02:50.405 --> 00:02:54.226
"Wow," Maggie whispered to Henry.

47
00:02:54.246 --> 00:02:57.827
"John had a motive we didn't know about!"

48
00:02:58.847 --> 00:03:00.588
The coach looked very serious.

49
00:03:01.708 --> 00:03:03.569
"Come with me, John," he said.

50
00:03:03.589 --> 00:03:17.079
"We'd better call your The next day Maggie and Henry were at the lemonade stand.

51
00:03:17.099 --> 00:03:21.502
"The last day of tryouts is almost over," Maggie said.

52
00:03:21.522 --> 00:03:24.884
"I wonder if Cole made the team."

53
00:03:25.985 --> 00:03:27.366
Suddenly they heard a shout.

54
00:03:27.386 --> 00:03:30.708
"That sounds like Cole," Henry said.

55
00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:33.245
Cole raced toward them, grinning.

56
00:03:33.265 --> 00:03:34.927
"I made it!"

57
00:03:35.287 --> 00:03:35.888
he cried.

58
00:03:35.908 --> 00:03:38.049
"I'm on the swim team!"

59
00:03:38.069 --> 00:03:42.833
"Congratulations!" Henry and Maggie exclaimed.

60
00:03:45.155 --> 00:03:46.817
They each gave him a high five.

61
00:03:46.837 --> 00:03:51.621
"Kyle must be mad that you got the spot," Maggie said.

62
00:03:51.641 --> 00:03:53.903
"Nope," Cole said.

63
00:03:53.923 --> 00:03:55.644
"He made it too!

64
00:03:56.565 --> 00:04:00.028
There was an extra spot after Coach Phillips kicked John off the team."

65
00:04:00.984 --> 00:04:03.746
"Then Daisy must be mad," Maggie said.

66
00:04:04.767 --> 00:04:05.508
Cole shrugged.

67
00:04:06.529 --> 00:04:07.129
"Not really.

68
00:04:08.571 --> 00:04:11.533
Her parents said she could take horseback-riding lessons instead."

69
00:04:11.553 --> 00:04:13.675
"What about Lauren?"

70
00:04:14.075 --> 00:04:15.176
Maggie asked next.

71
00:04:15.196 --> 00:04:17.798
"Is she mad that you made the team?"

72
00:04:18.859 --> 00:04:20.441
"Not anymore," Cole said.

73
00:04:20.461 --> 00:04:23.763
"I apologized again for saying she looked young.

74
00:04:24.744 --> 00:04:25.865
This time she listened."

75
00:04:26.926 --> 00:04:28.948
"That's great," Henry said.

76
00:04:30.344 --> 00:04:32.746
"Another great thing happened," Cole went on.

77
00:04:32.766 --> 00:04:36.890
"John's parents gave me the frogs John brought to the pool!

78
00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:40.633
They wanted to apologize for John trying to get me in trouble.

79
00:04:41.633 --> 00:04:44.316
They even gave me free frog food for one month!"

80
00:04:44.336 --> 00:04:47.899
"That's really generous," Henry said.

81
00:04:48.879 --> 00:04:52.102
Cole put his hand in his pocket and pulled out a five-dollar bill.

82
00:04:53.503 --> 00:04:54.244
"I almost forgot.

83
00:04:55.205 --> 00:04:59.088
Coach Phillips was really grateful that The Lemonade Detectives solved the mystery.

84
00:05:00.012 --> 00:05:01.833
He offered to pay our detective fee."

85
00:05:02.814 --> 00:05:04.355
Maggie looked away for a second.

86
00:05:05.336 --> 00:05:06.617
Then she looked back at Cole.

87
00:05:06.637 --> 00:05:10.159
"You didn't really do much to solve the case.

88
00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:13.142
Plus you got all those free frogs.

89
00:05:14.623 --> 00:05:17.685
So Henry and I should just split the money between the two of us."

90
00:05:17.705 --> 00:05:20.407
"What?" Cole protested.

91
00:05:20.427 --> 00:05:22.268
"That's not fair!"

92
00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:27.272
"The Lemonade Detectives are a team, Maggie," Henry reminded her.

93
00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:31.782
"But I've almost got enough money to start horseback-riding lessons!"

94
00:05:32.143 --> 00:05:32.963
Maggie argued.

95
00:05:32.983 --> 00:05:35.445
"I need money too!"

96
00:05:35.865 --> 00:05:36.466
said Cole.

97
00:05:37.506 --> 00:05:39.328
While they were arguing, a man walked over.

98
00:05:39.348 --> 00:05:42.170
"Would you like to buy some lemonade?"

99
00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:43.270
Henry asked.

100
00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:46.172
"No, thanks," the man said.

101
00:05:46.192 --> 00:05:49.835
"My son Kyle told me you three are pretty good detectives."

102
00:05:50.895 --> 00:05:52.597
"That's right," Maggie said.

103
00:05:52.617 --> 00:05:54.978
"Do you have a case for us?"

104
00:05:56.479 --> 00:05:57.360
The man sighed.

105
00:05:58.348 --> 00:06:02.934
"Yes. My wife's birthday is this weekend, and I forgot where I hid her gift."

106
00:06:04.016 --> 00:06:04.937
Henry smiled.

107
00:06:05.958 --> 00:06:09.443
Finding a lost birthday gift wasn't the most exciting case in the world.

108
00:06:10.444 --> 00:06:11.426
But that didn't matter.

109
00:06:11.446 --> 00:06:15.952
The Lemonade Detectives solved all mysteries, large or small!
